timestamp=2026-11-04T12:04:12.342Z level=INFO run=282380a7 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\nimport csv\n\nwith open('/app/dataset/hospital_compensation_registry.csv') as f:\n    reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n    rows = list(reader)\n\n# These claims suggest someone died. Let us trace:\n# PAT_033 (patient) has bereavement compensation. The emergency contact is PAT_011.\n# So probably PAT_033's close relation/insured died? Or maybe PAT_033 is the deceased? \n# Usually bereavement compensation goes to family members after someone dies.\n# Also family support adjustment - could be related to death/dependency changes.\n\n# Or look: who is the \"emergency_contact_patient_id\" in these cases? \n# Also check if the patient_id in the claim row is the beneficiary or the deceased?\n# Another interpretation: \"compensation_reason\" like bereavement means the claim is due to death of someone - maybe the patient themselves died? Unusual. Or maybe the emergency contact receives compensation when patient dies? Or the other way around.\n\n# Also see amounts - large lump sums (100k). And family support adjustment also large.\n# Look at \"emergency_contact_patient_id\" - maybe if patient is deceased, their emergency contact files/receives?\n\n# Let us look at who is contacting whom. Also look for patterns in other claims.\n# For example, PAT_033 files bereavement claim with contact PAT_011. Is there any claim where PAT_011 is mentioned differently?\n# Also see PAT_265 files family support adjustment, contact is PAT_065.\n# Look up PAT_065 - they have no claims, no coverage status. PAT_011 has claim and is active.\n# Another case: life event claim by PAT_006, contact PAT_078. Both have data?\n\nfor pid in ['PAT_011', 'PAT_065', 'PAT_078']:\n    matches = [r for r in rows if r['patient_id'] == pid]\n    for m in matches:\n        print(f'{pid}: claim={m[\"compensation_reason\"]}, contact={m[\"emergency_contact_patient_id\"]}, status={m[\"coverage_status\"]}')\n    print('---')\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
