timestamp=2026-11-04T12:05:17.503Z level=INFO run=282380a7 message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\nimport csv\n\nwith open('/app/dataset/hospital_compensation_registry.csv') as f:\n    reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n    rows = list(reader)\n\n# Case 3: PAT_006 has life event claim, contact PAT_078. Who lists PAT_078? And who does PAT_078 list?\n# PAT_078 is emergency contact for PAT_006 only? From earlier: listed_as_contact['PAT_078'] gave ['PAT_006']\n# Also look at PAT_078's contact: PAT_078's emergency_contact is PAT_011.\n# And PAT_011 is contact for others including PAT_078 and PAT_033.\n# PAT_006 also has coverage status active and large payment for life event. Interesting.\n\n# Another thought: maybe the \"patient\" who died is the emergency contact? \n# If PAT_033 is emergency contact for children/dependents, and PAT_033 died, then the children would list PAT_033 as contact but PAT_033 is deceased. Also bereavement might be filed.\n# That fits: dependents still have PAT_033 as their listed emergency contact. And there's a bereavement claim associated.\n\n# Similarly, if PAT_065 is a parent/guardian who died, then PAT_265 (and others?) list PAT_065 as contact. And PAT_265 has family support adjustment + inactive status - maybe PAT_265 is the surviving spouse or adult child? Or is PAT_265 also a dependent?\n\n# Also check Case 3: PAT_006 has life event claim, contact is PAT_078. And PAT_078's contact is PAT_011. Is PAT_078 the deceased? Let us look at who lists PAT_078 as contact - only PAT_006. And PAT_078 themselves are active with their own claim. That seems less clear. Or maybe PAT_011 (who is contact of PAT_078) is deceased? Because PAT_011 is also contact of PAT_033 (who has bereavement). That connects them.\n\n# Also look at the full web of connections.\n# PAT_011 is emergency contact for: ['PAT_078', 'PAT_033', 'PAT_167']\n# PAT_033 has bereavement claim + is listed as contact for 4 people (PAT_129, PAT_221, PAT_174, PAT_069). And PAT_033 lists PAT_011 as contact.\n# If PAT_033 died, that explains bereavement claim under PAT_033? Or explains why bereavement compensation is mentioned. Also dependents list PAT_033 as contact.\n# Similarly, if PAT_011 died, maybe PAT_033 (who lists PAT_011 as contact) and others who list PAT_011 as contact are affected? Also PAT_078 lists PAT_011 as contact - and PAT_006 (who is a dependent of PAT_078?) lists PAT_078 as contact. So PAT_006 is dependent of PAT_078; PAT_078 is dependent of/connected to PAT_011?\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
